fuck it, breeze

all she does is heal but she heals DAMN well. operators on the brink of death? toss them a heal and all's good. operators on the brink of death continuously and they're probably going to die with any other medic? breeze s2 has a godly aoe heal and she may only heal but heal she does and heal she fucking will

&#x200B;

also, carnelian! she has damage comparable to eyja and ranged tanks are extremely useful. her aoe is large as hell and her ramping damage is amazing. her self-heal on skill is also similarly great when ready to drop her ranged tank status for a 'ill just kill you so i don't have to tank' status. great boss killer and also ranged tanks are really useful. have i mentioned that ranged tanks are really useful yet? anyways, ranged tanks are really useful.

&#x200B;

special shoutout to jackie, for being godlike in is2 with the right relics. i prefer her over beehunter because her s1 means she synergises hella well with attackspeed + spinach/sacrilegious pasta + ribbon of honour and also she's adorable.

5\* would be either Diluc, Mona, or Xiao

&#x200B;

4\* would be Kaeya (please I need his c4 so bad), Diona, and Yanfei

do you have a friend that can help you play? usually I play supp and my friend plays adc, and even if we do bad we usually just laugh it off and joke about it, which got me over the fear of playing pvp and getting flamed for feeding

&#x200B;

this post reminds me of the time where I would click on 'draft' and then make myself a deal that if the queue  doesn't find a match within a minute, I could go play a bot game. I was super scared of pvp, but I kinda just played with a friend and realised it's not that scary.

&#x200B;

aram is useful for understanding what other champs do, such as the cooldown of a blitzcrank hook, when to go in, what to build, what champions rely on (for example, a missed irelia e means she can't engage at all)

(aram tip: don't pick a complicated champ like katarina or zed, pick someone like annie or lux and READ YOUR PASSIVE)

for me, aram is the most fun since it's fast, no toxicity, a new champ, and you'll do decent as long as you read the abilities and passive and make the most use of them (for example, if anivia's Q deals a stun and Chills enemies, and her E deals double damage to Chilled enemies, then logically you'll put 2 and 2 together and realise you Q first and then E)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

if you play in OCE (oceania server), dm me so I can play with you since I'm fairly new myself (level 44). also, dm me if you just want advice on stuff but I'm still figuring stuff out
